\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Derived a clusterwise Coulomb replacement estimate with an explicit near/far distinction. No N-body Hodge/operator analysis for general toric hyper-Kahler quotients is constructed.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied complete definition, catalogue wording, scope qualifications and source list for this canonical ID. The original-source citations are inherited as supplied references; no fresh primary-source or novelty search was performed for this attempt. No current open-status claim is inferred from this calculation.

\paragraph{A quantitative cluster replacement.}Partition positive point charges into clusters \(C_\alpha\). For each cluster choose its weighted center \(c_\alpha=M_\alpha^{-1}\sum_{j\in C_\alpha}m_ja_j\), total mass \(M_\alpha\), radius \(R_\alpha=\max_{j\in C_\alpha}|a_j-c_\alpha|\), and second moment \(Q_\alpha=\sum_{j\in C_\alpha}m_j|a_j-c_\alpha|^2\). At a point with \(d_\alpha=|x-c_\alpha|>R_\alpha\), Taylor's theorem and the Coulomb Hessian norm \(2/|y|^3\) give
\[\left|\sum_{j\in C_\alpha}\frac{m_j}{|x-a_j|}-\frac{M_\alpha}{d_\alpha}\right|\le\frac{Q_\alpha}{(d_\alpha-R_\alpha)^3}.
\]
The linear term cancels by the center definition. Summing gives a uniform error for replacing all sufficiently distant clusters by their centers. If \(d_\alpha\ge2R_\alpha\), the corresponding term is at most \(8Q_\alpha d_\alpha^{-3}\).
\paragraph{A genuine multiscale limitation.}A point close to one cluster may be far from the others. The estimate then permits replacing only the distant clusters while retaining the nearby potential exactly. Replacing every cluster at once would fail near a cluster center, where the denominator vanishes and the individual poles remain resolved. This is the elementary cluster hierarchy needed before an N-body-style partition of the ends can work.
\paragraph{Gap.}The bound is for scalar Coulomb potentials, not the Laplacian or Hodge operator of a general toric hyper-Kahler quotient. To use it in cohomology one must construct compatible coordinate/gauge charts in overlapping cluster regions, prove metric derivative bounds, and control operator domains and thresholds there. None of those analytical steps follows from the multipole estimate. The source's methodological programme is therefore unresolved; a Gibbons--Hawking toy model is explicitly kept separate from the full quotient class.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked weighted-center cancellation, second-moment error, separation constants and failure of simultaneous collapse near an unresolved cluster. This was an LLM adversarial audit, not independent human verification; no theorem prover was used. Prompts A then B applied to this ID: Checked weighted-center cancellation, second-moment error, separation constants and failure of simultaneous collapse near an unresolved cluster. Scope remains limited: Build compatible cluster charts and metric/operator estimates on quotient ends, including overlaps and threshold/domain control.

Coordinator checked the cluster-centered Taylor bound and its restriction to sufficiently distant clusters. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local shell used to read supplied files and serialize this manuscript; mathematics derived symbolically in the text, with no numerical experiment or formal proof assistant. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Build compatible cluster charts and metric/operator estimates on quotient ends, including overlaps and threshold/domain control.

